  "as_of_notes": "Counts represent registered (pre-registered shown separately) voters as of April 1, 2026, per the MN SOS 'Voter Counts by County' table on the Voter Registration Counts page. Pre-registered voters are 16-17 year olds who have applied and will become registered at 18; they are NOT included in 'total_registered'. Statewide total 3,827,205 registered; 90,129 pre-registered. Minnesota has same-day/Election-Day registration, so totals change daily; this is a point-in-time snapshot. Captured via Internet Archive snapshot dated 2026-04-13 of the SOS page because sos.mn.gov is behind a bot-mitigation (Radware) gateway that blocks direct automated fetches.",
  "data_quality": "high",
  "notes": "Minnesota does not register voters by political party (open primaries), so registers_by_party=false and all by_party fields are null. All 87 counties present. County registered-voter figures sum exactly to the SOS-stated statewide TOTAL of 3,827,205 (verified). FIPS codes assigned from standard Census MN county FIPS (state 27). 'pre_registered' included as an extra informational field per county; not part of total_registered. More recent precinct-level spreadsheets on the SOS page are dated May 1, 2025 and June 1, 2025; the April 1, 2026 county table is newer and is the latest official statewide-by-county count published."
}